<%- include('partials/header', { title, user, isPortalAdmin: true }) %>

<link rel="stylesheet" href="/admin-settings.css?v=<%= typeof assetVersion !== 'undefined' ? assetVersion : '0' %>" />

<section class="panel narrow">
  <div class="row-between">
    <h2>Welcome &mdash; first-run setup</h2>
    <a class="ghost" href="/admin/settings">Skip to advanced settings</a>
  </div>
  <p class="subtle">
    You're signed in as the break-glass administrator. Three quick steps will
    get the portal ready for end users. You can repeat or revisit any of them
    later from the Settings page.
  </p>

  <ol class="setup-steps">
    <li class="setup-step">
      <div class="setup-step-header">
        <span class="setup-step-number">1</span>
        <h3>Rotate the break-glass password</h3>
      </div>
      <p>
        The default break-glass password is well-known and meant only for the
        very first login. Replace it now and store the new value in your
        password vault.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="ghost" href="/admin/settings?tab=security">Go to Security &rarr; Break-Glass Admin</a>
      </p>
    </li>

    <li class="setup-step">
      <div class="setup-step-header">
        <span class="setup-step-number">2</span>
        <h3>Connect a directory</h3>
      </div>
      <p>
        Choose one or both directories the portal should manage. You can come
        back later to add the other side.
      </p>
      <ul class="setup-options">
        <li>
          <strong>Active Directory</strong>
          &mdash; on-prem managedBy ownership for security and distribution
          groups.
          <a class="ghost" href="/admin/settings?tab=directory#ad">Configure AD</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Microsoft Entra ID</strong>
          &mdash; cloud-owned groups via Microsoft Graph (OAuth + PKCE).
          The in-page wizard walks the app-registration steps for you.
          <a class="ghost" href="/admin/wizards/entra-directory/1">Configure Entra</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="subtle">
        Each integration card has its own <em>Test connection</em> button and
        <em>Save</em> button. Save only enables when the test passes (or when
        you leave the integration disabled).
      </p>
    </li>

    <li class="setup-step">
      <div class="setup-step-header">
        <span class="setup-step-number">3</span>
        <h3>Decide who else can administer the portal</h3>
      </div>
      <p>
        Break-glass should remain reserved for emergencies. Grant ongoing
        admin rights to one or more AD or Entra groups so day-to-day changes
        run under regular identities (and show up in the audit log with a
        real actor).
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="ghost" href="/admin/settings?tab=security">Go to Security &rarr; Delegated Admins</a>
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="subtle setup-footnote">
    Once at least one directory is enabled this welcome page is no longer
    shown. You'll land straight on the regular <a href="/admin/settings">Settings</a> page after every sign-in.
  </p>
</section>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
